== DESIGN (one mechanism, no second render path) ==
- wave_telegraph.gd (NEW, 144 ln): telegraph_step() after every mission.step
  diffs (phase_kind, wave); build -> paint, non-build -> _clear(); paint
  groups the wave rows by (spawner, enemy_id, kind) SUMMING counts, mounts
  SPRITE_BANK.make_sprite(enemy_id, ICON_H) billboards (the ONE bank; all 7
  shipped enemy ids already on TEXTURES — data leg pins the telegraph can
  never silently drop one) + WORLD_TEXT.make_text(count) (G6's DECLARED
  world-text mechanism; the Label3D-walk in test_damage_numbers stays green).
  GROUND/AIR distinction: an entry rides its lane's spawn HEIGHT — the raw
  waypoint[0].y (ground 0.0 / air 2.5) — so air previews float above the
  ground stack at the same gate, mirroring the altitude their lane spawns at.
  Entries are children of the telegraph node itself (fx cleanup doctrine);
  probe reads `shown`/`shown_total` plain vars (fx counter idiom).
- mission.tscn APPEND-ONLY: load_steps 8->9, ext row uid://7cf4beti21gb
  (engine-generated sidecar — Godot --import rc0 produced wave_telegraph.gd
  .uid, tscn row copied FROM the sidecar byte, never hand-typed), node
  "WaveTelegraph" last. Probe .uid sidecar likewise engine-generated
  (uid://bviv2foof0ddh).
- Kit godot/sim/g3_wave_telegraph_probe.gd (212 ln, g1 boot idiom + G6/v5
